<title>CHILE: Escondida June copper output down sharply on May.</title>
<headline>Escondida June copper output down sharply on May.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Minera Escondida Limitada reported the following copper and gold production figures for June:</p>
<p>COPPER (metric tonnes)	  June 1997  May 1997  June 96</p>
<p>Copper in concentrates	  68,021     113,840   62,833</p>
<p>Copper cathodes		    5,985	 6,157    4,079</p>
<p>Total				 74,006     119,997   66,912</p>
<p>			    January-June 1997   January-June 1996</p>
<p>Total				480,348		  408,839</p>
<p>					June 1997	   June 1996</p>
<p>GOLD (ounces)			15,551		  13,162</p>
<p>NOTE: Minera Escondida is owned by Broken Hill Proprietary and RTZ Corp plc.</p>
<p>((--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
